From 536f5fc7019f814c8429964ea6e9dfe97b3dbc46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:03:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/41] Gate and MIDI clock outputs keep going under an
 external MIDI clock (upstream 7d9beeef)

Following an external clock, the Deluge's gate clock output and MIDI clock output stopped after
a short burst: their scheduling ran on the internal timer ticks (lastTimerTickActioned,
nextTimerTickScheduled), which stand still while the clock comes from outside. They are now also
scheduled from every incoming clock tick, on its time base (computeExternalClockSchedule(): at
most one immediate tick, then a resync if behind), and the gate clock's level follows the tick
count's parity after a resync, so edge-triggered followers don't see half the rate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
